  <conditions attached="1">
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consistent with the Article III of the SBAA [or the Supplemental Provisions to the Project Document], the responsibility for the safety and security of the Implementing Partner and its personnel and property, and of UNDP&#x2019;s property in the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s custody, rests with the Implementing Partner.  To this end, the Implementing Partner shall: a)	put in place an appropriate security plan and maintain the security plan, taking into account the security situation in the country where the project is being carried; b)	assume all risks and liabilities related to the Implementing Partner&#x2019;s security, and the full implementation of the security plan.</narrative>
   </condition>
   <condition type="1">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social and environmental sustainability will be enhanced through application of the UNDP Social and Environmental Standards (http://www.undp.org/ses) and related Accountability Mechanism (http://www.undp.org/secu-srm).</narrative>
   </condition>
  </conditions>
  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sq.m of land cleared;
Number of training services provided by ANAMA to other mine affected countries;
ANAMA passed through UNMAS certification (Y/N).</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2017">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">448 mln sq.m land cleared</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) 558 mln of land
2) Procurement of mine detectors and protection gear
3) 130,826 EOD risk education, these figures mentioned as target in the project document and as 84,000 in the proposal</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) During demining operations carried out from 01 January to 30.12.2021, 62,018,866 square meters of territory (6,201 hectares) were inspected, 4880 anti-personal and 2335 anti-tank mines, and 11,205 unexploded ordnance (UXO) were found and neutralized.

2) As technical support with the frame of ongoing restructuring and increase in staffing of ANAMA UNDP procured 150 sets of mine detectors and 150 PPE sets to equip newly recruited teams of deminers.

3) According to project description EORE activity also was supported in the framework of the UNDP support. ANAMA has a great experience in mine risk education. EORE conducting in 3 direction by ANAMA. One of it is to strength mine awareness at the schools located in war affected territories. It was purchased about 26 600 EORE books and handed overed to ministry of Education to strength awareness among teachers and pupils as well. This is also very useful to distribute 4-6 class methodology books for IDPs at the refugee camps in different regions of Azerbaijan whom planned to return homeland according to the future plan. Some of the books that purchased hand overed to vulnerable families that affected by war</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
